		array( 'order' => 9, 'slug' => 'dr-ali-thwaini', 'name' => 'Dr. Ali Thwaini', 'role' => 'Consultant Urologist', 'headline' => 'Consultant Urologist', 'specialty' => 'Urology, Andrology & Male Infertility', 'clinic' => 'Dubai', 'imageAlt' => 'Dr. Ali Thwaini', 'nationality' => 'British', 'languages' => 'English, Arabic', 'areasOfInterest' => 'Uro-oncology and laparoscopy; renal, prostate and bladder cancer; stone disease (endoscopic management including laser); prostate disease with minimally invasive treatment including laser and UroLift; andrology – male sexual dysfunction (including regenerative medicine and penile prosthesis), enhancement (penile enlargement); female urinary incontinence; and infertility.', 'education' => 'Medicine at Baghdad University, Iraq. Master’s degree from Queen Mary University of London, UK. Intercollegiate Specialty Board Certificate in Urology (FRCS-Urology). Fellowship of the Royal College of Surgeons (FRCS) Ireland (1999). Jordanian Board of Urology (2000). Arab Board in Urology (2001).', 'bio' => 'Dr Ali Thwaini is a Consultant Urologist with a special interest in urological cancers, namely renal cancers. Dr Ali was the lead for renal cancers at the Belfast Health and Social Care Trust (Belfast City Hospital, Northern Ireland). His main skills are in advanced laparoscopy and renal cancer and renal reconstruction procedures. Dr. Ali is also an Honorary Clinical Lecturer at Queens University, Belfast, with over 40 Medline publications in the field. After completing his degree, Dr. Ali relocated to Jordan where he started his career in Urology at the Royal Medical Services, then moved to Abu Dhabi where he worked for three years as a specialist at SKMC. In 2004 he moved to the UK, finished his MD from Queen Mary University of London, and entered the UK national higher training scheme in Urology in Northern Ireland. He completed training in 2012 with FRCS-Urology and CCT UK-wide accreditation.' ),
		array( 'order' => 10, 'slug' => 'dr-gautam-allahbadia', 'name' => 'Dr. Gautam Allahbadia', 'role' => 'Consultant', 'headline' => 'Consultant Reproductive Medicine and Infertility', 'specialty' => 'Assisted Reproduction & IVF', 'clinic' => 'Dubai', 'imageAlt' => 'Dr. Gautam Allahbadia', 'nationality' => 'Indian', 'languages' => 'English, Urdu', 'areasOfInterest' => 'Assisted Reproduction Techniques (ART), IVF, IVF Lite, PGT-A, PGT-M, and ultrasound-guided embryo transfers.', 'education' => 'MD – Obstetrics & Gynaecology from Lokmanya Tilak Municipal Medical College and General Hospital (1990). Diplomat of National Board (DNB) in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, FNAMS, FCPS – Mid. & Gynae, DGO, D.F.P, FICMU, FICOG, MBBS.', 'bio' => 'Dr Gautam Allahbadia is a Medical Professional with over 25 years expertise of Assisted Reproductive Techniques. Dr. Gautam is a noted world-authority on Ultrasound Guided Embryo Transfers and one of the pioneers in Minimal Stimulation IVF (IVF Lite) in South-East Asia. He has authored over 150 scientific papers, 134 book chapters and 27 textbooks, the latest of which is a comprehensive text, entitled “Minimal Stimulation IVF”. He is currently the Editor Emeritus of the Journal of Obstetrics & Gynaecology of India & the IVF Lite (Journal of Minimal Stimulation IVF). Throughout his career, Dr. Gautam Allahbadia has been instrumental in developing new fertility-enhancing protocols and propagating the use of Ultrasound in Embryo Transfer procedures. He is the recipient of over 25 prizes & fellowships, including the Canadian Young Scientist Fellowship Award (1994), the Deutscher Akademischer Austauschdienst Fellowship (1996) for IVF/ICSI training at the University of Gottingen in Germany, and the FOGSI-CORION National Research Award (1998). Dr. Gautam was elected Vice President of the World Association of Reproductive Medicine (WARM) and named “Mumbai’s Top Doc” for 2012 by peer nomination.' ),
